{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29839 - PROTEIN:4970",
  "verbalization": "Pseudopterosin Q appears to exert its biological effects through a series of interconnected pathways that ultimately target CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence suggests that Pseudopterosin Q directly interacts with Thioredoxin, a mitochondrial protein, which in turn is targeted by Yuanhunine and Oleamide. Both Yuanhunine and Oleamide are known to modulate cellular processes that influence CCRF-HSB-2, a human cancer cell line. Additionally, Pseudopterosin Q is linked to Caspase-5, which is targeted by 5-Oxobrucine, and 5-Oxobrucine also affects CCRF-HSB-2. These findings collectively imply that Pseudopterosin Q may act through multiple downstream targets, potentially modulating cellular signaling pathways that influence CCRF-HSB-2. The integration of these pathways highlights a complex, multi-tiered mechanism by which Pseudopterosin Q could interact with CCRF-HSB-2, though the exact nature of the molecular interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
